    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Moderate persistent asthma, well controlled (J45.40)</content>. Asthma Control Test 22. Spirometry has normalized: FEV1 3.98 L (89 percent predicted) and FEV1/FVC 0.79, up from 3.20 L and 0.67 at intake. Peak flow 605 L/min today. He has been well controlled for about two months. [S]<list><item>Continue budesonide-formoterol two inhalations twice daily and one as needed.</item><item>Action plan reset to his personal best of 610 L/min: green 488 or above, yellow 305 to 487, red below 305.</item><item>Consider stepping down at the six-month review if control holds and there are no exacerbations.</item><item>Next spirometry in one to two years unless control changes.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Asthma Control Test</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>22, well controlled</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Spirometry</td><td>At diagnosis, 3 to 6 months after stabilization, then every 1 to 2 years</td><td>Completed today</td><td>FEV1 3.98 L, 89 percent predicted; FEV1/FVC 0.79; FVC 5.02 L</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Peak flow and personal best</td><td>Daily or with symptoms for moderate to severe asthma</td><td>Completed today</td><td>605 L/min in clinic; personal best 610 L/min</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Inhaler technique with his own device</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Correct</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Adherence and reliever use</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Full adherence; reliever before training only</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Exacerbation history</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>None since starting controller therapy</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Trigger and exposure review, smoking and vaping status</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Bedding covers in place; never smoker</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Written asthma action plan</td><td>Every visit and after every exacerbation</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Zones reset to the confirmed personal best</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Step-up or step-down assessment</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Controlled for about two months; reassess for step-down at the six-month review</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>FeNO and blood eosinophils</td><td>As indicated</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Phenotyping completed at the four-week review; no diagnostic uncertainty</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Biologic candidacy assessment</td><td>Only if severe and uncontrolled despite optimized Step 4 to 5 therapy</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Well controlled at Step 4</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Vaccination status</td><td>Yearly</td><td>Up to date</td><td>PCV20 given at the four-week review; influenza vaccine due in the autumn</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Asthma Control Test score of 20 or more by the three-month review. Outcome by 2026-06-08: ACT rose from 13 to 22 [S]</item><item>FEV1 of 80 percent predicted or more on spirometry after stabilization. Outcome by 2026-06-08: FEV1 89 percent predicted with a normal FEV1/FVC ratio [S]</item><item>No exacerbation needing oral corticosteroids over the six months after starting controller therapy. In progress; target 2026-09-14 [S]</item><item>Return to full boxing and rowing training without limiting symptoms. Outcome by 2026-06-08: Training fully by the three-month review, using one reliever inhalation before sessions [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: Global Strategy for Asthma Management and Prevention, 2025 update (2025); 2020 Focused Updates to the Asthma Management Guidelines: A Report from the National Asthma Education and Prevention Program Coordinating Committee Expert Panel Working Group (2020); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, asthma monograph (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Asthma review in three months, or within one week of any exacerbation. Next scheduled visit 2026-09-14: six-month asthma review after a summer exacerbation. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
